# Ultrasound LMA Macro — Fiji/ImageJ

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-Fiji%20%2F%20ImageJ%201.x-green)](https://fiji.sc/)
[![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-3.1.0-blue)](CHANGELOG.md)
[![DOI](https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX.svg)](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX)

> A semi-automated Fiji/ImageJ macro for measuring **Longissimus dorsi muscle area (LMA)**, subcutaneous fat thickness, and muscle depth from ultrasound images — keyboard-driven, no fixed image naming required.

Developed as part of a precision livestock technology research pipeline (UESPI / UNIVASF / UIUC). Applicable to any ruminant species with ultrasound images of the *m. Longissimus dorsi*.

