## Features

| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| 🗂️ Flexible metadata | No filename pattern required — enter Subject, Group, and Replicate freely at each session |
| 📐 Scale calibration | Draw any reference line, enter its real-world length and unit (cm / mm / in) |
| 🫀 LMA measurement | Polygon or freehand ROI → area, perimeter, circularity |
| ✂️ Spline smoothing | Optional contour regularization via cubic spline fitting |
| 📌 ROI Manager | Save traced contours for review and export |
| 🔬 Fat thickness | Three subcutaneous fat measurements + automatic mean |
| 📏 Muscle depth | Dorsal–ventral anatomical depth of the *m. Longissimus dorsi* |
| 💾 Structured CSV | One file per Group value, auto-header, one row per image |
| ⌨️ Keyboard-only | F1 – F9, no menus needed during analysis |
| 🛡️ Guard rails | Blocks measurement steps if scale is not calibrated |
| 🖥️ Cross-platform | Windows, macOS, and Linux |

---

## Requirements

- [Fiji](https://fiji.sc/) — any recent release (ImageJ 1.x bundled)
- No additional plugins required

---

## Installation

**Method 1 — Current session only**

1. Download [`LMA_Macro.ijm`](LMA_Macro.ijm)
2. In Fiji: **Plugins → Macros → Install…** → select the file

**Method 2 — Persistent (auto-loads with Fiji)**

Copy `LMA_Macro.ijm` to your Fiji `macros/` folder and restart Fiji:

| OS | Path |
|----|------|
| Windows | `C:\Fiji.app\macros\` |
| macOS | `/Applications/Fiji.app/macros/` |
| Linux | `~/Fiji.app/macros/` |

---

## Workflow

### Keyboard shortcuts

| Key | Command | Action |
|-----|---------|--------|
| **F1** | Init | Open metadata dialog, reset session |
| **F2** | Set Scale | Calibrate scale from a drawn reference line |
| **F3** | Measure LMA | Trace muscle ROI → area, perimeter, circularity |
| **F4** | Measure Fat | Three subcutaneous fat thickness measurements |
| **F5** | Measure Depth | Dorsal–ventral muscle depth measurement |
| **F6** | Save Results | Append row to CSV, reset for next image |
| **F7** | Status | Show current session state |
| **F8** | Reset | Clear measurements (saved CSVs untouched) |
| **F9** | Open Folder | Open CSV output folder in file manager |

### Step-by-step

```
Open image
     │
     ▼
F1 — Init
     Dialog opens with three editable fields:
       Subject / Animal ID        →  "Animal01", "Sheep_15", "Ewe07" ...
       Group / Session / Treatment →  "Control", "Session02", "Week04" ...
       Replicate / Scan           →  "1", "Rep2" ...
     If the filename matches a common pattern, fields are pre-filled.
     Edit as needed — any text is accepted.
     │
     ▼
F2 — Set Scale
     Draw a line over a reference of known length.
     Enter the real-world length and choose the unit (cm / mm / in).
     │
     ▼
F3 — Measure LMA
     Trace the Longissimus dorsi contour (Polygon Selection recommended).
     Optional: spline smoothing · save ROI to ROI Manager.
     │
     ▼
F4 — Measure Fat  (×3 prompts)
     Draw three perpendicular lines across the subcutaneous fat layer.
     │
     ▼
F5 — Measure Depth
     Draw one line from the dorsal to the ventral muscle border.
     │
     ▼
F6 — Save Results
     Row appended to CSV · session cleared · open next image → F1
```

### Recovering from mistakes

| Situation | Solution |
|-----------|----------|
| Wrong LMA tracing | **F8** → re-trace → **F3** |
| Wrong fat measurement | **F8** → **F4** (fat always resets at F4 start) |
| Wrong depth | **F8** → **F5** |
| Wrong row already saved | Open the CSV in a text editor and delete that row |

---

## Metadata and Output

### The metadata dialog (F1)

Every image starts with a fully editable dialog:

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Image Metadata  —  LMA Macro v3.1.0             │
│  File: A1C1_1.jpg                                │
│                                                  │
│  Subject / Animal ID         [ Animal_1        ] │
│  Group / Session / Treatment [ Collection_01   ] │
│  Replicate / Scan            [ 1               ] │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Fields are pre-filled when the filename matches a recognizable pattern, but always editable. There is no required naming convention.

### Adapting to your experiment

| Study design | Subject | Group | Replicate |
|-------------|---------|-------|-----------|
| Repeated collections | `Animal_05` | `Collection_2` | `1` |
| Diet treatment trial | `Sheep_12` | `HighProtein` | `Rep1` |
| Breed comparison | `Animal_03` | `Dorper` | `2` |
| Longitudinal | `Ewe_07` | `Week04` | `1` |

### Output files

One CSV is created per unique **Group** value:

```
lma_Collection_01.csv
lma_Control.csv
lma_HighProtein.csv
lma_results.csv        ← if Group is left blank
```

### CSV columns

| Column | Unit | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `image_file` | — | Original filename (captured at Init) |
| `subject` | — | Subject / Animal ID |
| `group` | — | Group / Session / Treatment |
| `replicate` | — | Replicate / Scan number |
| `lma_area_cm2` | scale unit² | Longissimus dorsi cross-sectional area |
| `lma_perimeter_cm` | scale unit | Muscle contour perimeter |
| `lma_circularity` | 0–1 | Shape circularity (1 = perfect circle) |
| `fat1_mm` – `fat3_mm` | scale unit | Individual fat thickness measurements |
| `fat_mean_mm` | scale unit | Mean subcutaneous fat thickness |
| `muscle_depth_mm` | scale unit | Anatomical depth, dorsal–ventral axis |

> Column names use `cm` / `mm` by convention. Actual values are in whichever unit you set at F2.

---

## FAQ

**Can I use this for cattle, goats, or other species?**  
Yes. The macro measures whatever you trace and accepts any experimental design.

**My images have a different naming convention — will it work?**  
Yes. Any filename is accepted. The F1 dialog may or may not pre-fill the fields depending on the pattern, but you can always type manually.

**What if a CSV value shows `-999999`?**  
That is the internal sentinel for "not measured." Delete that row, re-open the image, and start from F1.

**How do I reset the output folder?**  
Run this snippet via **Plugins → Macros → Evaluate…**:
```javascript
call("ij.Prefs.set", "lma.out_dir", "");
```

**Does it work with DICOM stacks?**  
Only on the currently active frame. Navigate to the target frame before pressing F1.

**Why are the column names `cm` / `mm` if I can choose any unit?**  
The column names are fixed for CSV consistency. The values reflect whichever unit you set at F2.

